course: dictionary
lesson: 1225
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Check the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues.
explain: «On the farm, the bull stood by the gate while the calf stayed close to its mum.» The farm and the calf tell you that a bull is the adult male cow.
explain: «Her arrow hit the bull's-eye, the very centre of the target.» Here the target tells you that bull's-eye means the centre of a target, not an animal.
fact: A word with more than one meaning is a multiple-meaning word. The context tells you which meaning is being used.
fact: A bull is an adult male cow. It can also be the male of some other big animals, such as elephants, whales and seals.
fact: The bull's-eye is the centre of a target, and it scores the most in many games and sports.
fact: The plural of bull is bulls. A calf is the baby of a cow.
fact: Some cave paintings in France and Spain show bulls, and some are over 30,000 years old.
exercise: On the farm, the bull stood by the gate. What is a bull? | *An adult male cow | A type of tree | A baby cow | A small dog
exercise: «Her arrow hit the bull's-eye.» What does bull's-eye mean? | *The centre of a target | A sweet from the shop | A kind of farm gate | A hole in the fence
exercise: A bull can be the male of some other big animals. Which one is it? | Robin | *Elephant | Rabbit | Hen
test: In the countryside, you must never enter a field with a bull. Why? | *Bulls can charge and are very dangerous | Bulls like to be stroked | Bulls are slow and sleepy | Bulls only eat grass in the morning
test: «Take the bull by the horns» is a phrase. What does it mean? | Run away from a problem | *Face a problem bravely | Eat your dinner quickly | Ask someone else to help
exam: «Bulls cannot tell red from green; it is the movement of a cape that makes them charge.» What makes a bull charge? | Bright sunshine | The colour red | The sound of a gate | *The movement of a cape
